# http headers for llm discovery
# this is for llms not humans
#
# headless ai fetchers (claude code, cursor, future chatgpt browse) read the
# Link response header and skip the html body. json-ld doesnt reach them, only
# wire-level signals do
#
# activates on cloudflare pages and netlify. github pages ignores this file
# entirely so today none of these rules actually fire. the html <link> tag and
# the .md endpoints are doing the real work right now
# easiest fix without leaving github pages: a cloudflare worker / transform
# rule on the existing zone. or move to cloudflare pages and these activate
# automatically
#
# .md endpoints are emitted by src/pages/[...path].md.ts

# default on every url, points at the studio-wide llms.txt + llms-full.txt
/*
  Link: </llms.txt>; rel="alternate"; type="text/plain"; title="LLM context", </llms-full.txt>; rel="alternate"; type="text/markdown"; title="Full LLM context"
  Vary: Accept

# per-route Link header pointing at the matching .md
# matching rules combine, so the default above and the per-route rule below
# both fire on the same request

